  m_Name: ConstantMeshGearBoxData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Constant Mesh Gear Box
  engineDescription: 'A Constant Mesh Gear Box is a type of gearbox in which all
    the gears are always in mesh with their corresponding gears. The gears on the
    main shaft rotate freely, and power is transmitted by engaging dog clutches with
    the required gear. This arrangement prevents direct sliding of gears and reduces
    wear.

    In a constant mesh gearbox, different gear ratios are obtained by
    locking the desired gear to the shaft through a dog clutch. The gears remain
    continuously engaged, while shifting is achieved by connecting the selected gear
    to the shaft. It is widely used in automobiles and motorcycles because it provides
    smoother and quieter gear operation.'
  engineCategory: Engineering
